                <pb facs="0782" n="684" xml:id="pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/2939: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Guggenheim</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-29T15:00:00-05:00">December 29, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:08 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>177. Authorities closed Habana Yacht Club yesterday afternoon, alleging that
                    building was being used as meeting place by persons conspiring against the
                    Government. This measure affects only the best social element among whom it has
                    engendered increased bitterness toward Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Guggenheim</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
